\section*{Question 1}

Let \(R\) be the shaded region bounded by the graphs of \(y=\sqrt{x}\) and \(y=e^{-3 x}\) and
\begin{itemize}
\item[] the vertical line \(x=1\), as shown in the figure above.
\item[(a)] Find the area of \(R\).
\item[(b)] Find the volume of the solid generated when \(R\) is revolved about the horizontal line \(y=1\).
(c) The region \(R\) is the base of a solid. For this solid, each cross section perpendicular to the \(x\)-axis is a rectangle whose height is 5 times the length of its base in region \(R\). Find the volume of this solid.
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/eaaeb13d-db8c-4e14-99f4-c3c5ba1875a2-1.jpg?height=374&width=385&top_left_y=417&top_left_x=1603)
\end{itemize}

Point of intersection
\[
e^{-3 x}=\sqrt{x} \text { at }(T, S)=(0.238734,0.488604)
\]
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text { Area } & =\int_{T}^{1}\left(\sqrt{x}-e^{-3 x}\right) d x \\
& =0.442 \text { or } 0.443
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(b)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text { Volume } & =\pi \int_{T}^{1}\left(\left(1-e^{-3 x}\right)^{2}-(1-\sqrt{x})^{2}\right) d x \\
& =0.453 \pi \text { or } 1.423 \text { or } 1.424
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(c)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \text { Length }=\sqrt{x}-e^{-3 x} \\
& \text { Height }=5\left(\sqrt{x}-e^{-3 x}\right) \\
& \text { Volume }=\int_{T}^{1} 5\left(\sqrt{x}-e^{-3 x}\right)^{2} d x=1.554
\end{aligned}
\]
\end{itemize}

